rely  has to be answered by the prime minister  the foreign secretary and the home  secretary the plans just weren't there  well i think two things i mean firstly  there was some of it foreseen because  when i raised myself back in june the  whole question of afghan interpreters  and actually to be fair to the  government i'm not i said sometimes i'm  happy to be critical when i need to be  but to be fair to the government between  me asking my question on on the order  paper and between the home secretary  answering it they made a policy a policy  of of actively trying to help  people to be interpreters for our armed  forces and so on what they that issue  has been around for years yeah yeah but  nevertheless you know when i pressed  they moved um and that was a few months  ago but the problem yeah and part of the  problem is that nobody forcible i think  even the most pessimistic and i'm  probably amongst those nobody foresaw  the sheer speed of collapse of the  afghan government if somebody come on  your program a month ago and say and  said in a month's time the taliban will  be in charge  you would have heard them i mean most  people have thought they were wrong  that's what's happened a large part the  responsibility for that i'm afraid is  down to the two consecutive american  presidents the way they handle it but  nevertheless we can't do anything about  that now the issue now is to get on top  of it i agree it would be better if we'd  had more advanced plans laid  but remember in the middle of the copic  crisis as well other things distracting  people  it would have been better now we have to  move fast what that says i can move fast  if canada can move fast if the americans  say they can take thirty thousand now  they're gonna they're gonna need to take  at least three times that amount by the  way but if they can say that now if  the canadians can move then we're gonna  have to move a bit faster than five  thousand money here  can we just talk about a time scale um  reference has been made to the syrian  refugee resettlement scheme where the uk  promised to take 20 000 refugees over  five years what kind of time scale are  we looking at for the refugees of  afghanistan because for them time is of  the essence the taliban have been in  control of the country officially  probably since sunday  we've seen the absolute chaos  around the kabul airport of people  trying to get out they are frightened of  the taliban they will say they haven't  got  five years they fear that the taliban  will be searching for them and hunting  them down within the coming weeks and  months  i agree  and i think  to compare it with  the syrian scheme is just  irrelevant frankly  the people are going to come we're going  to come in five minutes not not five  years um and our problem  is going to be how we cope  with the at the new afghan authorities  um uh whilst we're trying to extract  people from their grip  and that's not going to be easy it's not  going to be easy but we've got to do it  you know and it won't show up in some  business school textbook we have to use  our brain and do it for ourselves  so what's that going to look like  because the practicalities of this  situation are very difficult here on the  programme yesterday afternoon i spoke to  a gentleman called pen farthing um a  former serving soldier in afghanistan  who now runs an ngo in the country an  animal charity and he spoke to us on the  phone and he said  at the time he couldn't find his wife  and a heavily pregnant colleague who had  gone to the airport who couldn't even  get into the airport even though the  advice from the british government when  they made contact with the embassy was  to get to the airport to get one of  those evacuation flights they couldn't  even get into the airport so there's  a practical element at the moment that  the government need to sort out and does  that involve more troops going what does  that look like because that's going to  have to be the first step surely it may  well do and i understand that um  an aircraft british aircraft left this  morning with almost no peak money  because they couldn't get them through  the bearings now  that's good that's going to take uh some  pretty heavy duty administration too so  it may well mean more troops go out it  also may mean some pretty robust  conversations with the new afghan  government uh and we're going to have to  do that  and put some fine ways of putting  pressure on  we're going to have to talk to our  allies this is this is a very very  difficult task we've got to do  but it either happens now or it doesn't  happen but if we're still predicting  about it in six months time we probably  failed  and you know they're going to be they're  going to be people who work for us  directly uh obviously translators but  other people do drivers and other people  they're going to be indirect people  people work and contract as far as uh  they're going to be people who feel at  risk for it because of politics they're  going to be women who worked  in the open as it were and are now being  sent home there'll be a  a potentially vast number of people and  we have to uh get across those practical  issues we also need to to talk to our  allies very carefully to make sure that  that  those who are not under pressure can  help us out and there may be some so so  it's not an easy task i agree with you  it would have been ideal if we planned  it all out last year but you would have  had to have a degree of prescience in  the middle of a covert crisis uh to do  that and get the resources right our  government no government in the world  really had that presence  uh we've now got to move very fast to  make up for it uh otherwise the next  time we have a foreign policy excursion  of any sort um people are going to be  very very thoughtful indeed before they  actually help uh our armed forces and so  it's not just in their interest it's not  just a matter of  of  i was going to say christian charity  probably the wrong phrase but but  charity it's a matter of actually doing  our duty to the people who helped

